PASS tempus: both ends open with profile 1
PASS tempus: the handshake completes
PASS tempus: the server's facts say the profile's ALPN was selected
PASS tempus: the client's facts say the profile's ALPN was selected
PASS tempus: the server reads the client's public key (the node's)
PASS tempus: the client reads the server's public key (the sentinel's)
PASS tempus: the key read is not some other identity's
PASS a trust/1 client is refused by a tempus/1 server (no common ALPN)
PASS a tempus/1 client is refused by a trust/1 server (no common ALPN)
PASS two credentials: all four ends open
PASS two credentials: the TRUST handshake completes
PASS two credentials: the TEMPUS handshake completes
PASS two credentials: the TEMPUS client sees the bridge's TEMPUS key
PASS two credentials: the TEMPUS server sees the node's key
PASS two credentials: the TRUST client does not see a TEMPUS key
PASS two credentials: the TRUST connection's ALPN bit is set (trust/1)
PASS two credentials: a later TEMPUS open keeps the first TEMPUS credential (the node's, the bridge's)
PASS a P-256 peer: the handshake completes
PASS a P-256 peer: its key is refused (not Ed25519)
PASS a profile that does not exist is refused
PASS a negative profile is refused
PASS the key of a connection with no peer certificate yet is refused
PASS the key of a handle that is not a connection is refused
all passed
exit=0
